        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1ecbcf04-90a7-59b7-bdac-8a43288db23a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Degville, Richie Furay, Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, Dewey Martin, Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, Randy Meisner, Tony James, Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper\n- Organizations: Sigue Sigue Sputnik, Buffalo Springfield, Poco, Rock & Roll Hall of Fame, EMI\n- Products: \"Love Missile F1-11\", Dress for Excess\n- Places: Walsall\n- Events: Blitz Kids\n\nFacts:\n- Richie Furay was born on May 9, 1944.\n- Martin Degville was born on January 27, 1961, in Walsall.\n- Richie Furay is an American singer, songwriter, and Rock & Roll Hall of Fame member.\n- Richie Furay is best known for co-founding Buffalo Springfield with Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, and Dewey Martin.\n- Richie Furay is also best known for co-founding Poco with Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, and Randy Meisner.\n- Martin Degville later became the frontman of Tony James' band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Martin Degville is the lead singer and co-songwriter of the UK pop band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper, and Martin Degville were among the attendees associated with Blitz Kids.\n- Sigue Sigue Sputnik had a worldwide hit single in 1986 with \"Love Missile F1-11\" and released six other EMI singles.\n- Dress for Excess is the second album by the British band Sigue Sigue Sputnik, and it was released in 1988.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
